## Bashan OS — LibreOffice with Qt6/KDE integration.
## Verified in trixie: there is NO LibreOffice UI translation for Kurmanji,
## Sorani or Syriac, so those three get the English office UI (documented in
## docs/I18N.md and stated in the installer).

libreoffice-writer
libreoffice-calc
libreoffice-impress
libreoffice-draw
libreoffice-base
libreoffice-math

# Native Qt6 + KDE file dialogs and theming
libreoffice-qt6
libreoffice-kf6

# Metric-compatible substitutes for Arial/Times/Courier, so documents from
# Word open with the right line breaks
fonts-liberation2

# UI translations that exist upstream
libreoffice-l10n-es
libreoffice-l10n-de
libreoffice-l10n-fr
libreoffice-l10n-pt
libreoffice-l10n-ru
libreoffice-l10n-el
libreoffice-l10n-ar
libreoffice-l10n-he
libreoffice-l10n-fa

# Spellcheck. Verified in trixie by installation candidate, not just by name:
#   - Persian DOES have one, as myspell-fa (LibreOffice reads myspell
#     dictionaries through dictionaries-common). This corrects the Stage 1
#     assumption that Persian had no dictionary.
#   - Kurmanji has NO LibreOffice-usable dictionary. hunspell-ku does not
#     exist; only aspell-ku does, and LibreOffice does not use aspell.
#   - Sorani and Syriac have no dictionary of any kind.
hunspell-en-us
hunspell-es
hunspell-de-de
hunspell-fr
hunspell-pt-pt
hunspell-pt-br
hunspell-ru
hunspell-el
hunspell-ar
hunspell-he
myspell-fa
